    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51470" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Xĕnŏcrătes</span></b> ,
			is, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ξενοκράτης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a disciple of Plato</i>, <i>born at
				Chalcedon in the 95th Olympiad</i>, B. C. 400,
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 1, 4, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc.
				5, 18, 51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Off. 1, 30, 109</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rep. 1,
				2, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A sculptor</i>, <i>a pupil of
				Tisicrates</i>, <i>and author of works on
				sculpture</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8, 19, §
			83</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A writer on the art of painting</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				10, 36, § 68</span></i>.</div>
